  "body": "Fixes #182 after review.\n\nThe current full-model TLM underfeeds resident SC tiles: the latest FFN defers next-wave DMA until array completion, while the shared SRAM fabric is only16GB/s. This change adds a bounded DMA-prefetch schedule with an explicit response buffer and protects the single resident weight bank through computation/restoration. It provides a standard Micron DDR4-1866 two-channel/two-rank DRAMSys profile and an8MiB64-bank/64GB/s SRAM profile with a widened local receiver; legacy configurations remain reproducible. Digital matrix tile sizes stay fixed during SC-engine sweeps.\n\nValidation completed:72 mechanism/regression checks,3 full36-layer Qwen3-4B Link ablations,8 actual DRAMSys throughput checks and2 tiny integrated DRAMSys gates. Current same-Link times:1412.979ms baseline,1343.787ms prefetch only,879.748ms SRAM widening only. Full DRAMSys11-case Slurm2913 is running; final results and source/artifact SHA records will be added to this same PR before delivery.\n\nThis is synthetic batch1 decode timing/traffic analysis, not new PPL or silicon PPA. The DMA buffer, full-width weight macro, wider interconnect and several FFN operators remain uncharacterized; total area/energy stays unknown. DRAMPower covers the audited core-current profile, not PHY/I/O/controller power. No automatic merge. Projects synchronization is pending missing read:project scope.\n\nEntry:architecture_tlm/unified_v6/MEMORY_HIERARCHY_ZH.md; handoff:work/jieruiz/182/HANDOFF.md. Main baseline5273e5d9; frozen full-model execution7e44b6a4.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-10-25T03:25:10Z",
